WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.123
- He's yours.

00:00:01.123 --> 00:00:01.956
- Ah.

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:04.510
- But you didn't even say anything.

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:07.202
- That's right, no winterns.

00:00:07.202 --> 00:00:09.150
(audience laughs)

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.330
I played that perfectly and kept quiet.

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:13.200
And keeping quiet is not easy for me.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.820
I mean, you guys know I'm not allowed back

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.899
into three movie theaters.

00:00:16.899 --> 00:00:17.732
(audience laughs)

00:00:17.732 --> 00:00:19.040
Kenney gets the hand off.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:20.600
Oo, to the 10.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.070
She's at the five.

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:25.140
She's got one man to beat and scores.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.001
Touchdown!

00:00:28.001 --> 00:00:30.883
(audience cheers)

00:00:30.883 --> 00:00:32.210
- Well, I guess that answers the question

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:35.043
of whether Carols still has her real hips.

00:00:35.043 --> 00:00:38.424
(laughing)
(applauding)

00:00:38.424 --> 00:00:39.393
- All right, what's up?

00:00:39.393 --> 00:00:42.307
I'm back with Patricia Heaton, y'all.

00:00:42.307 --> 00:00:44.173
(audience cheers)

00:00:44.173 --> 00:00:47.340
That was a clip from her
new show, Carol's Second Act

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.580
which airs Thursdays on CBS.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:51.550
So you say your life kinda mirrors Carol,

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:52.690
it mirrors Carol's a bit right?

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.330
- Yeah 'cause her kids
are out of the house.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.370
My kids are out of the house.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:57.680
She's embarking on this
new adventure as a doctor.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:59.420
She used to be a high
school science teacher.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:02.840
She's divorced so she's
reframing her life.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:05.210
It's new for me in the
sense that I'm first time

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.320
exec producing the show
and there's a lot of

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.090
responsibilities that come with that.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:09.923
- Yeah.

00:01:10.787 --> 00:01:11.960
- And it's good 'cause
it's challenging me.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.870
I am kind of stress dreams.

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:17.164
Where I'll be like in a
house that I'm remodeling

00:01:17.164 --> 00:01:19.470
and I don't know if it's working

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.580
and it's costing a lot of money and I know

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:24.190
that's like a reflection
of trying to build a show.

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:25.023
- Yes.

00:01:25.023 --> 00:01:25.900
- You know, like can I do this?

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:27.171
Is it gonna look good?

00:01:27.171 --> 00:01:30.760
So it's good though,
keeps your brain going.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:31.593
- Active, yeah, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:31.593 --> 00:01:33.440
- No I'm the same way, I've
never done anything like this.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:34.273
- Right, it's a lot.

00:01:34.273 --> 00:01:36.152
- It's a whole different
level of pressure.

00:01:36.152 --> 00:01:37.052
(laughs)
- Right.

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:40.290
- I'm just kidding, I'm just kidding.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:42.893
- That's vodka in here, just
in case you're wondering.

00:01:42.893 --> 00:01:43.830
(laughs)
- Yeah.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:46.150
- But you are raising, this is crazy

00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:47.619
and I can't believe I didn't know this

00:01:47.619 --> 00:01:49.850
'cause that's an injustice for how hard

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:51.100
you must have been working,

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.480
but you raised four toddlers while doing

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:54.313
Everybody Loves Raymond?

00:01:54.313 --> 00:01:56.400
- The first season of Raymond,
I had a three year old,

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.670
a one year old and I was
pregnant with the third.

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:00.670
And then the third season I had my fourth.

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:02.430
All c-sections.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.910
And I don't know how,
because now working on Carol

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:07.360
with no kids at home, I'm exhausted.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.440
How I did it with four kids.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.187
I used to get up in the morning
and my first thought was,

00:02:12.187 --> 00:02:14.296
"I could really use a beer right now".

00:02:14.296 --> 00:02:15.390
(laughs)

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:17.060
Just thinking about
getting through the day.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:18.765
- Just a tiny bit.

00:02:18.765 --> 00:02:20.170
- And when I got home, you
know I'd get the boys to bed.

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:22.168
I'd pour a big glass
of red wine, you know.

00:02:22.168 --> 00:02:23.341
- Yes, I do.

00:02:23.341 --> 00:02:24.880
- And one night, I was drinking the wine

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:26.780
and my son Joe called me back upstairs

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:29.600
so I ran up, I leaned down and
I said, "What is it honey?"

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:30.867
And he just looked at me, he said,

00:02:30.867 --> 00:02:33.057
"Mom you smell like communion".

00:02:33.943 --> 00:02:36.026
(laughs)

00:02:37.953 --> 00:02:39.760
It's 'cause I go down there

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:42.179
and pray for you boys every night.

00:02:42.179 --> 00:02:44.097
- I'm such a good mom.

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:44.930
(laughing)

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.540
I used to love communion
'cause I'd be starving during

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:49.870
church and they'd pass
out those little crackers,

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:51.220
and I'm like, I didn't
feel the Lord enough,

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:54.200
just one more, just little more.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.033
(laughing)

00:02:55.033 --> 00:02:56.190
You weren't supposed to,
I'm probably going to hell,

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:57.023
it's fine.

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:59.500
So where are your sons these days?

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:02.421
- So, the two oldest are in Nashville.

00:03:02.421 --> 00:03:04.098
- [Kelly] Yes, you were
just talking about that.

00:03:04.098 --> 00:03:05.900
- Yeah, so my oldest
son is in a band called

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:08.930
Forest Fire Gospel
Choir, they're very good.

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:09.763
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:03:09.763 --> 00:03:10.596
- But he also works at Adele's.

00:03:10.596 --> 00:03:11.540
Did you ever eat at Adele's?

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:12.373
- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:12.373 --> 00:03:15.180
- The second one is still
living there also, just working.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:16.520
Third one's here in L.A.

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:20.391
Fourth one is at The Ohio State
University, my alma mater.

00:03:20.391 --> 00:03:21.320
- Oh that's exciting.
- Do we have any

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:22.153
Buckeye's here?

00:03:22.153 --> 00:03:24.450
O-H, O-H?
(audience member whoos)

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:25.283
- Not one.
- I-O.

00:03:25.283 --> 00:03:26.150
You have to say I-O.

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:27.958
Okay not a single Buckeye.
- Anybody love Texas?

00:03:27.958 --> 00:03:28.791
Anybody?

00:03:28.791 --> 00:03:30.520
(cheers)
Okay, there we go.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.400
- Yeah, so we're adjusting but it's great.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.663
I love when they come home, yeah.

00:03:33.663 --> 00:03:34.496
- That's fun though.

00:03:34.496 --> 00:03:36.070
I always feel like my husband's
looking forward to it.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:38.170
We have a three year old and
he's still looking forward

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:39.080
to it.
- Oooo.

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:40.770
- [Kelly] Like he's like
it's gonna be so exciting.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:43.274
- Three is a wonderful
age and boys are just--

00:03:43.274 --> 00:03:44.290
- It is a threenager though,
but yeah that's our boy.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.360
- He's a threenager?
- Yeah, we call it.

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:50.600
Two's were fine, three's
are the devil has actually

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:53.500
come inside their body
and I need an exorcist.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.270
- So you're drinking
communion every night?

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:56.863
- I drink a lot of communion.

00:03:56.863 --> 00:03:57.834
(laughs)

00:03:57.834 --> 00:03:59.250
It wasn't my fault.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:00.750
Jesus changed that water into wine.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.700
He taught us correctly.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.296
Yes, I only need water.

00:04:04.296 --> 00:04:06.620
Are you bothering them to
have grandkids yet, though

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:07.650
because now they're out of the house?

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:10.270
- Oh yes and in fact,
I do it nationally like

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:13.600
every talk show I go on, okay
what camera should I look in?

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:14.980
This one right here, okay boys,

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:18.040
I'm just letting you know,
the first one that gives me

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:20.610
a grandchild gets the house.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:21.879
(audience cheers)

00:04:21.879 --> 00:04:22.962
- Oh my gosh.

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:27.490
- I just got them all outta the house

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:28.800
and now I want more back in.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.340
- I know, I want more kids.

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:32.143
My husband doesn't,
it's super interesting.

00:04:32.143 --> 00:04:33.580
(laughs)

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:36.660
Speaking of kids, tell us about
your work with World Vision.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:37.520
You do a lot of work with them.

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:39.860
- Yeah, and that's a lot apart
of my second act I think.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:42.020
The biggest provider of
clean water in the world

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:44.530
and they started the sponsorship program

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:45.660
where you can sponsor a child

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.430
but they've done this cool new thing now

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:48.580
called Chosen.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:51.430
And it's $39 a month but
instead of World Vision

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:53.270
just sending you a picture
of a child and saying,

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:54.420
would you like this child,

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:56.700
you send your picture to World Vision

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:58.780
and they take it into a community

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:03.023
and they put all the pictures
up and the child picks you.

00:05:03.023 --> 00:05:03.951
(audience awws)

00:05:03.951 --> 00:05:06.540
And then you get a letter
from the child telling you

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:07.760
why they picked you.

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:10.030
It's really rewarding,
it's really exciting.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:11.740
- And consistency with one person.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:12.922
- [Patricia] That's right.

00:05:12.922 --> 00:05:14.394
- I think that's so, kids,
I mean you know this better

00:05:14.394 --> 00:05:15.760
than anyone with four kids
but they need consistency.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:17.550
- Well and I've traveled
a lot with World Vision.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:20.640
To Zambia, Jordan, Uganda,
Rwanda and you know,

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.130
people are the same everywhere.

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:24.620
I was traveling with one
of the World Vision workers

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:27.310
from Rwanda and you're in
the car for a long time.

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:29.200
He was telling me about
having to go home that weekend

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.810
and go to the wedding of
one of his wife's coworkers.

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:33.190
And he was complaining
'cause like I don't know

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:34.970
any of these people at her office.

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:36.751
- It's like what happens at home.

00:05:36.751 --> 00:05:39.110
- I'm like, it doesn't
matter if you're in Africa

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:41.950
or the U.S., like marriage
is the same everywhere.

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:44.387
- No one wants to go to
the office Christmas party.

00:05:44.387 --> 00:05:47.022
I'm just kidding, ours
is gonna be awesome guys.

00:05:47.022 --> 00:05:48.820
(laughs)

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:49.690
- But I think it just shows you,

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:51.520
how we're really all the same everywhere

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:53.140
and this World Vision Chosen program

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:54.210
is a great way to connect.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:55.147
- Has your child picked
you yet for World Vision?

00:05:55.147 --> 00:05:58.140
- No, I have not heard of
who my child is yet, yes.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:05:59.340
- [Kelly] Okay, that's so interesting.

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:00.220
- Yeah, I'm waiting too.

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:03.250
- Well, we asked World Vision
for the video of your child,

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:04.083
would you like to see

00:06:04.083 --> 00:06:05.327
who chose you?
- Oh you have it?

00:06:05.327 --> 00:06:06.831
- Yes.
- Oh my God.

00:06:06.831 --> 00:06:08.935
- Yes, let's take a look.
(audience applauds)

00:06:08.935 --> 00:06:12.068
(in foreign language)

00:06:12.068 --> 00:06:14.818
(peaceful music)

00:06:38.084 --> 00:06:40.910
(audience applauds)

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:42.577
- That was so sweet.

00:06:43.508 --> 00:06:44.729
- And I love little boys.

00:06:44.729 --> 00:06:46.810
Okay, I don't need a
grandchild right away.

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:47.647
- He picked you and said your smile was--

00:06:48.889 --> 00:06:49.722
- Oh my God.
- Oh my gosh,

00:06:49.722 --> 00:06:50.850
that was so sweet.

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:51.997
That was really special.
- That's amazing.

00:06:51.997 --> 00:06:55.040
- You guys, we all gotta do
that, that was so special.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:58.190
- It's a great thing to
do as a Christmas gift

00:06:58.190 --> 00:06:59.023
to yourself.

00:06:59.023 --> 00:07:00.071
You get a lot more back.

00:07:00.071 --> 00:07:01.550
- My mother does that at Christmas.

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:04.160
She'll give us, like I
bought a cow for this family.

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:05.780
- That's right, World Vision has a catalog

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:07.700
where if you can't sponsor a child,

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:10.300
maybe just, you can buy
chickens for a family.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:11.470
- She does that, my mama.
- Yes they share it

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:12.620
with the rest of the village.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:14.200
It's a gift that keeps on giving.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.033
It's wonderful.

